is allows the model to learn a stable mapping from generic visual features to bird species labels without overfitting or disrupting the pretrained representations. In the second phase, the upper layers of the backbone are selectively unfrozen and fine-tuned with a substantially lower learning rate. This enables the network to adapt higher-level features to the specific structure of spectrogram data while preserving the robustness of lower-level representations, typically resulting in improved generalization performance.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"base_resnet.trainable = True\nfor layer in base_resnet.layers[:-30]:\n    layer.trainable = False\n\nmodel_resnet.compile(\n    optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=1e-3),\n    loss=tf.keras.losses.SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(),\n    metrics=[\n        \"accuracy\",\n        tf.keras.metrics.SparseTopKCategoricalAccuracy(k=5, name=\"top5_acc\")\n    ]\n)\n\nhistory_ft = model_resnet.fit(\n    train_ds_224,\n    validation_data=val_ds_224,\n    epochs=30,\n    callbacks=callbacks\n)\n\nmodel_resnet.evaluate(test_ds_224)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-21T12:33:41.895325Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-21T12:33:41.896089Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-21T13:44:59.862051Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-12-21T12:33:41.896063Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-21T13:44:59.861238Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Epoch 1/30\n\u001b[1m14487/14487\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1051s\u001b[0m 71ms/step - accuracy: 0.9296 - loss: 0.3921 - top5_acc: 0.9868 - val_accuracy: 0.0426 - val_loss: 10.1327 - val_top5_acc: 0.2094 - learning_rate: 0.0010\nEpoch 2/30\n\u001b[1m14487/14487\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1017s\u001b[0m 70ms/step - accuracy: 0.9714 - loss: 0.1393 - top5_acc: 0.9974 - val_accuracy: 0.0556 - val_loss: 9.5015 - val_top5_acc: 0.3057 - learning_rate: 0.0010\nEpoch 3/30\n\u001b[1m14487/14487\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1019s\u001b[0m 70ms/step - accuracy: 0.9769 - loss: 0.1157 - top5_acc: 0.9978 - val_accuracy: 0.0550 - val_loss: 9.9505 - val_top5_acc: 0.3813 - learning_rate: 0.0010\nEpoch 4/30\n\u001b[1m14487/14487\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1049s\u001b[0m 72ms/step - accuracy: 0.9799 - loss: 0.1057 - top5_acc: 0.9981 - val_accuracy: 0.0657 - val_loss: 9.7378 - val_top5_acc: 0.4298 - learning_rate: 0.0010\n\u001b[1m1762/1762\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m141s\u001b[0m 80ms/step - accuracy: 0.0023 - loss: 10.6642 - top5_acc: 0.1502\n","output_type":"stream"},{"execution_count":62,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"[9.501509666442871, 0.05559597536921501, 0.30573350191116333]"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":62},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*For some reason at this point the notebook crashed and we did not have enough time to run the whole notebook again. For that reason the output from this point on is screenshoots from a previous run which was successful using the code as displayed*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#evaluate again\n\nmodel_resnet.evaluate(test_ds)\n\nhistory_frame = pd.DataFrame(history_ft.history)\n\n# Loss curve\nhistory_frame[['loss', 'val_loss']].plot()\nplt.title(\"Loss\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Epoch\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Loss\")\nplt.show()\n\n# accuracy curve\nhistory_frame[['accuracy', 'val_accuracy', 'top5_acc', 'val_top5_acc']].plot()\nplt.title(\"Accuracy & Top-5 Accuracy\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Epoch\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Score\")\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.194390Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.194713Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.194530Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.194544Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"![image.png](attachment:4f2a4377-e529-4d7b-a3bf-9924ca2259ef.png)","metadata":{},"attachments":{"4f2a4377-e529-4d7b-a3bf-9924ca2259ef.png":{"image/png":""},"639b70d8-ceed-4c83-8ce5-b33c402b93a3.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2.4.5 Build an ensemble\n\nWhen looking at examples of other people working on this task we observed, that many of them used ensembles of models, for example the winning team combined 10 model: https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/birdclef-2021/writeups/dr-1st-place-quick-solution\n\nWe thought this makes sense, at this might help with identifiying and balancing weak spots. However limitations are, that we only had 3 models to start with, which also did not have an as strong baseline performance.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# align shapes\nIMG_SIZE = 224\n\ndef to_224(x, y):\n    x = tf.image.resize(x, (IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE))\n    return x, y\n\ntest_ds_224 = test_ds.map(to_224, num_parallel_calls=tf.data.AUTOTUNE)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.195724Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.196017Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.195879Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-21T13:55:35.195892Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"we could weight them differently, because cnn does not exactly have good results before...\nBut since all accuracies are only moderate we do not want to make it unnecessarily complicated here, as it will not lead to a dramatically improved performance.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def predict_proba(model, ds):\n    return model.predict(ds, verbose=0)  # (N, C)\n\np_cnn    = predict_proba(model_cnn,    test_ds)\np_effnet = predict_proba(model_effnet, test_ds_224)\np_resnet = predict_proba(model_resnet, test_ds_224)\n\n\np_ens = (p_cnn + p_effnet + p_resnet) / 3.0\ny_pred = np.argmax(p_ens, axis=1)","metadata":{"trus